###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018031
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018031> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                            rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018033> ;
                                            owl:inverseOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018032> ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> "pyruvate anion (CHEBI:15361) is the conjugate base of the neutral pyruvic acid (CHEBI:32816)" ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A is a direct conjugate base of B if and only if A is chemical entity that is a Brønsted–Lowry Base (i.e., can receive a proton) and by receiving a particular proton transforms it into B." ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002575> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018033> ;
                                            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> <https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4423-4370> ;
                                            rdfs:label "is direct conjugate base of" ;
                                            rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/oborel/obo-relations/issues/643> .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018032
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018032> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                            rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018034> ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> "neutral pyruvic acid (CHEBI:32816) is the conjugate acid of the pyruvate anion (CHEBI:15361)" ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A is a direct conjugate acid of B if and only if A is chemical entity that is a Brønsted–Lowry Acid (i.e., can give up a proton) and by removing a particular proton transforms it into B." ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002575> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018034> ;
                                            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> <https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4423-4370> ;
                                            rdfs:label "is direct conjugate acid of" ;
                                            rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/oborel/obo-relations/issues/643> .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018033
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018033> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                            rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018030> ;
                                            owl:inverseOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018034> ;
                                            rdf:type owl:TransitiveProperty ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> "(E)-cinnamoyl-CoA(4-) (CHEBI:57252) is a deprotonated form (E)-cinnamoyl-CoA (CHEBI:10956), which involves removing four protons." ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> """A is a deprotonated form of B if and only if A is chemical entity that is a Brønsted–Lowry Base (i.e., can receive a proton) and by adding some nonzero number of protons transforms it into B.

This is a transitive relationship and follows this design pattern: https://oborel.github.io/obo-relations/direct-and-indirect-relations.""" ;
                                            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> <https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4423-4370> ;
                                            <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "obo:chebi#is_conjugate_base_of" ;
                                            rdfs:label "is deprotonated form of" ;
                                            rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/oborel/obo-relations/issues/643> .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018034
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018034> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                            rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018030> ;
                                            rdf:type owl:TransitiveProperty ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> "(E)-cinnamoyl-CoA (CHEBI:10956) is a protonated form of (E)-cinnamoyl-CoA(4-) (CHEBI:57252), which involves adding four protons." ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> """A is a protonated form of B if and only if A is chemical entity that is a Brønsted–Lowry Acid (i.e., can give up a proton) and by removing some nonzero number of protons transforms it into B.

This is a transitive relationship and follows this design pattern: https://oborel.github.io/obo-relations/direct-and-indirect-relations.""" ;
                                            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> <https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4423-4370> ;
                                            <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "obo:chebi#is_conjugate_acid_of" ;
                                            rdfs:label "is protonated form of" ;
                                            rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/oborel/obo-relations/issues/643> .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018035
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018035> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                            rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018030> ;
                                            rdf:type owl:SymmetricProperty ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> "phenol (CHEBI:15882) and aniline (CHEBI:17296) are matched molecular pairs because they differ by one chemical transformation i.e., the replacement of aryl primary amine with aryl primary alcohol." ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> """A and B are a matched small molecular pair (MMP) if their chemical structures define by a single, relatively small, well-defined structural modification.

While this is normally called \"matched molecular pair\" in the cheminformatics literaturel, it is labeled as \"matched small molecular pair\" so as to reduce confusion with peptides and other macromolecules, which are also referenced as \"molecules\" in some contexts.

This relationship is symmetric, meaning if A is a MMP with B iff B is a MMP with A.

This relationship is not transitive, meaning that A is a MMP with B and B is a MMP with C, then A is not necessarily an MMP with C.""" ;
                                            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> <https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4423-4370> ;
                                            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/date> "2023-02-28T18:53:32Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
                                            <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym> "is MMP with" ,
                                                                                                           "is matched molecular pair with" ;
                                            rdfs:label "is matched small molecular pair with" .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018035> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> ;
   owl:annotatedTarget """A and B are a matched small molecular pair (MMP) if their chemical structures define by a single, relatively small, well-defined structural modification.

While this is normally called \"matched molecular pair\" in the cheminformatics literaturel, it is labeled as \"matched small molecular pair\" so as to reduce confusion with peptides and other macromolecules, which are also referenced as \"molecules\" in some contexts.

This relationship is symmetric, meaning if A is a MMP with B iff B is a MMP with A.

This relationship is not transitive, meaning that A is a MMP with B and B is a MMP with C, then A is not necessarily an MMP with C.""" ;
   <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.1002/ddr.21045> ,
                                     <https://doi.org/10.1021/jm200452d> ,
                                     <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matched_molecular_pair_analysis>
 ] .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018036
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018036> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                            rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018030> ;
                                            rdf:type owl:SymmetricProperty ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> "3-carboxy-3-mercaptopropanoate (CHEBI:38707) is tautomer of 1,2-dicarboxyethanethiolate (CHEBI:38709) because 3-carboxy-3-mercaptopropanoate is deprotonated on the carboxylic acid whereas 1,2-dicarboxyethanethiolate is deprotonated on the secondary thiol." ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> """Two chemicals are tautomers if they can be readily interconverted.

This commonly refers to prototropy in which a hydrogen's position is changed, such as between ketones and enols. This is also often observed in heterocyclic rings, e.g., ones containing nitrogens and/or have aryl functional groups containing heteroatoms.""" ;
                                            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> <https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4423-4370> ;
                                            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/date> "2023-03-18T23:49:31Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
                                            <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "obo:chebi#is_tautomer_of" ;
                                            <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym> "is desmotrope of" ;
                                            rdfs:label "is tautomer of"@en ;
                                            rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/oborel/obo-relations/issues/697> .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018036> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> ;
   owl:annotatedTarget "3-carboxy-3-mercaptopropanoate (CHEBI:38707) is tautomer of 1,2-dicarboxyethanethiolate (CHEBI:38709) because 3-carboxy-3-mercaptopropanoate is deprotonated on the carboxylic acid whereas 1,2-dicarboxyethanethiolate is deprotonated on the secondary thiol." ;
   rdfs:seeAlso <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_38707> ,
                <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_38709>
 ] .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018037
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018037> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                            rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018030> ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> "carboxylatoacetyl group (CHEBI:58957) is substituent group from malonate(1-) (CHEBI:30795)" ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "Group A is a substituent group from Chemical B if A represents the functional part of A and includes information about where it is connected. A is not itself a chemical with a fully formed chemical graph, but is rather a partial graph with one or more connection points that can be used to attach to another chemical graph, typically as a functionalization." ;
                                            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> <https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4423-4370> ;
                                            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/date> "2023-03-18T23:49:31Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
                                            <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "obo:chebi#is_substituent_group_from" ;
                                            rdfs:label "is substitutent group from"@en ;
                                            rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/oborel/obo-relations/issues/697> .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018037> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> ;
   owl:annotatedTarget "carboxylatoacetyl group (CHEBI:58957) is substituent group from malonate(1-) (CHEBI:30795)" ;
   rdfs:seeAlso <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_30795> ,
                <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_58957>
 ] .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018038
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018038> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                            rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018030> ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> "hydrocortamate hydrochloride (CHEBI:50854) has parent hydride hydrocortamate (CHEBI:50851)" ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> """Chemical A has functional parent Chemical B if there is chemical transformation through which chemical B can be produced from chemical A. 

For example, the relationship between a salt and a freebased compound is a \"has functional parent\" relationship.""" ;
                                            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> <https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4423-4370> ;
                                            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/date> "2023-03-18T23:49:31Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
                                            <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "obo:chebi#has_functional_parent" ;
                                            rdfs:label "has functional parent"@en ;
                                            rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/oborel/obo-relations/issues/697> .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018038> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> ;
   owl:annotatedTarget "hydrocortamate hydrochloride (CHEBI:50854) has parent hydride hydrocortamate (CHEBI:50851)" ;
   rdfs:seeAlso <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_50851> ,
                <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_50854>
 ] .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018039
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018039> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                            rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018030> ;
                                            rdf:type owl:SymmetricProperty ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> "dexmedetomidine hydrochloride (CHEBI:31472) is enantiomer of levomedetomidine hydrochloride (CHEBI:48557) because the stereochemistry of the central chiral carbon is swapped." ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> """Chemicals A and B are enantiomers if they share the same molecular graph except the change of the configuration of substituents around exactly one chiral center.

A chemical with no chiral centers can not have an enantiomer. A chemical with multiple chiral centers can have multiple enantiomers, but its enantiomers are not themselves enantiomers (they are diastereomers).""" ;
                                            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> <https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4423-4370> ;
                                            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/date> "2023-03-18T23:49:31Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
                                            <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "obo:chebi#is_enantiomer_of" ;
                                            <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym> "is optical isomer of" ;
                                            rdfs:label "is enantiomer of"@en ;
                                            rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/oborel/obo-relations/issues/697> .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018039> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> ;
   owl:annotatedTarget "dexmedetomidine hydrochloride (CHEBI:31472) is enantiomer of levomedetomidine hydrochloride (CHEBI:48557) because the stereochemistry of the central chiral carbon is swapped." ;
   rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_48557> ;
   rdfs:seeAlso <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_31472>
 ] .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018040
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018040> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                            rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018030> ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> "pyranine (CHEBI:52083) has parent hydride pyrene (CHEBI:39106). Pyrene is molecule with four fused benzene rings, whereas pyranine has the same core ring structure with additional sulfates." ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "Chemical A has parent hydride Chemical B if there exists a molecular graphical transformation where functional groups on A are replaced with hydrogens in order to yield B." ;
                                            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> <https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4423-4370> ;
                                            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/date> "2023-03-18T23:49:31Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
                                            <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "obo:chebi#has_parent_hydride" ;
                                            rdfs:label "has parent hydride"@en ;
                                            rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/oborel/obo-relations/issues/697> .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018040> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> ;
   owl:annotatedTarget "pyranine (CHEBI:52083) has parent hydride pyrene (CHEBI:39106). Pyrene is molecule with four fused benzene rings, whereas pyranine has the same core ring structure with additional sulfates." ;
   rdfs:seeAlso <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_39106> ,
                <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_52083>
 ] .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0019000
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0019000> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                            rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002410> ;
                                            rdfs:domain <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000015> ;
                                            rdfs:range <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0000001> ;
                                            owl:propertyChainAxiom ( <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002211>
                                                                     <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0019000>
                                                                   ) ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A relationship that holds between a process and a characteristic in which process (P) regulates characteristic (C) iff: P results in the existence of C OR affects the intensity or magnitude of C." ;
                                            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8688-6599> ;
                                            rdfs:label "regulates characteristic" .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0019001
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0019001> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                            rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0019000> ;
                                            owl:propertyChainAxiom ( <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002213>
                                                                     <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0019001>
                                                                   ) ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A relationship that holds between a process and a characteristic in which process (P) positively regulates characteristic (C) iff: P results in an increase in the intensity or magnitude of C." ;
                                            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8688-6599> ;
                                            rdfs:label "positively regulates characteristic" .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0019002
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0019002> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                            rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0019000> ;
                                            owl:propertyChainAxiom ( <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002212>
                                                                     <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0019001>
                                                                   ) ,
                                                                   ( <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002213>
                                                                     <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0019002>
                                                                   ) ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A relationship that holds between a process and a characteristic in which process (P) negatively regulates characteristic (C) iff: P results in a decrease in the intensity or magnitude of C." ;
                                            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8688-6599> ;
                                            rdfs:label "negatively regulates characteristic" .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0019003
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0019003> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ,
                                                     owl:IrreflexiveProperty ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> "Given individuals f, i, x, and y, where f is a 'molecular function', i is an 'information biomacromolecule', and x and y are instances of different types of gene products, if f 'enabled by' i within an OWL model of a biological pathway, and i 'has substitutable entity' both x and y, then either x or y are valid enablers of function f within the modeled biological context." ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "Relates one individual to another which is capable of standing in for the first individual in its other relations to other individuals." ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8688-6599> ;
                                            <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#inSubset> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/valid_for_gocam> ;
                                            rdfs:label "has substitutable entity"@en .


