###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/DOID_9970
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/DOID_9970> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                           rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/WOND_0000193> ;
                                           <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "An overnutrition that is characterized by excess body fat, traditionally defined as an elevated ratio of weight to height (specifically 30 kilograms per meter squared), has_material_basis_in a multifactorial etiology related to excess nutrition intake, decreased caloric utilization, and genetic susceptibility, and possibly medications and certain disorders of metabolism, endocrine function, and mental illness." ;
                                           rdfs:label "Obesity" ,
                                                      "obesity" .


