                                               rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ENVO_00001998> ;
                                               <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000111> "podzol" ;
                                               <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "Podzols are soils with a typically ash-grey upper subsurface horizon, bleached by loss of organic matter and iron oxides, on top of a dark accumulation horizon with brown, reddish or black illuviated humus and/or reddish Fe compounds. Podzols occur in humid areas in the boreal and temperate zones and locally also in the tropics." ;
                                               <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000412> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/envo.owl> ;
                                               rdfs:label "podzol" .


