###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000017
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000017> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                             rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000023> ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000111> "regulatory role"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> "Regulatory agency, Ethics committee, Approval letter; example:  Browse these EPA Regulatory Role subtopics  http://www.epa.gov/ebtpages/enviregulatoryrole.html  Feb 29, 2008"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000120> ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "a role which inheres in material entities and is realized in the processes of making, enforcing or being defined by legislation or orders issued by a governmental body."@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "GROUP:  Role branch"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "OBI, CDISC"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000232> "govt agents responsible for creating regulations; proxies for enforcing regulations.  CDISC definition:  regulatory authorities. Bodies having the power to regulate. NOTE: In the ICH GCP guideline the term includes the authorities that review submitted clinical data and those that conduct inspections. These bodies are sometimes referred to as competent"@en ;
                                             rdfs:label "regulatory role"@en .


