###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000021
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000021> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                             rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000030> ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000111> "list-mode data file"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> "An example of a list-mode data file is a file following list-mode Flow Cytometry Standard (FCS) format. Since FCS files can be in histogram mode or  list-mode we have to specify which data format specifically. List-mode format in the overwhelming (even universal) option used."@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125> ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A list-mode data file is a binary digital entity where events are stored sequentially, parameter by parameter."@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "One example of usage is in the context of flow cytometry, however is not restricted to this community and is more widely used, e.g. by imaging people."@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "person:Chris Stoeckert"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "group:Flow Cytometry community" ;
                                             rdfs:label "list-mode data file"@en .


