                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> "Precipitation is the formation of a solid in a solution during a chemical reaction. When the reaction occurs, the solid formed is called the precipitate, and the liquid remaining above the solid is called the supernate.  Wikipedia" ;
