                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A DNA sequencing by ligation assay that identifies sequence information using primers to hybridize to the P1 adapter sequence within the library template, fluorescently labeled di-base probes to compete for ligation to the sequencing primer, multiple cycles of ligation, detection and cleavage to determine the eventual read length, following a series of ligation cycles, the extension product is removed and the template is reset with a primer complementary to the n-1 position for a second round of ligation cycles."@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "Philippe Rocca-Serra" ;
