<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200064> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                             rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200085> ,
                                                             [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                               owl:onProperty <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000417> ;
                                                               owl:someValuesFrom <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200197>
                                                             ] ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000111> "centroid mass spectrum"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000123> ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A centroid mass spectrum is a data transformation in which many points are used to delineate a mass spectral peak, is converted into mass-centroided data by a data compression algorithm. The centroided mass peak is located at the weighted center of mass of the profile peak. The normalized area of the peak provides the mass intensity data."@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "Person:Tina Hernandez-Boussard"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000118> "centroid mass spectrum calculation" ,
                                                                                          "centroiding" ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "centroid mass spectrum"@en ;
                                             rdfs:label "centroid mass spectrum analysis"@en .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200066
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200066> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                             rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200073> ,
                                                             [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                               owl:onProperty <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000293> ;
                                                               owl:someValuesFrom <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000175>
                                                             ] ,
                                                             [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                               owl:onProperty <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000299> ;
                                                               owl:someValuesFrom <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0001265>
                                                             ] ,
                                                             [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                               owl:onProperty <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000417> ;
                                                               owl:someValuesFrom <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000791>
                                                             ] ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000111> "Holm-Bonferroni family-wise error rate correction method"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> "t-tests were used with the type I error adjusted for multiple comparisons, Holm's correction (HOLM 1979), and false discovery rate, http://www.genetics.org/cgi/content/full/172/2/1179" ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000120> ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "a data transformation that performs more than one hypothesis test simultaneously, a closed-test procedure, that  controls the familywise error rate for all the k hypotheses at level α in the strong sense. Objective: multiple testing correction"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> """2011-03-14: [PRS]. Class Label has been changed to address the conflict with the definition
Also added restriction to specify the output to be a FWER adjusted p-value

The 'editor preferred term' should be removed"""@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "Person:Helen Parkinson" ,
                                                                                          "Philippe Rocca-Serra"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holm%E2%80%93Bonferroni_method" ;
                                             rdfs:label "Holm-Bonferroni family-wise error rate correction method"@en .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200070
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200070> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                             rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200080> ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000111> "edge weighting"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000123> ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "Edge weighting is the substitution or transformation of edge length using numerical data.  Data input include a symmetric adjacency matrix for a network and a second data set, for example a list of interactor pairs and a confidence score associated with the experimental detection of each pair's interaction.  Each element in the adjacency matrix is transformed or replaced with the corresponding number in the second data set.  Output data are a modified adjacency matrix reflecting the transformed state of the network."@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "Tina Hernandez-Boussard"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "editor"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000232> """was classified under algorithm class which is not acceptable super-class
TO BE DEALT WITH STILL BY RICHARD.  JAMES"""@en ;
                                             rdfs:label "edge weighting"@en .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200071
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200071> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                             rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200169> ,
                                                             [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                               owl:onProperty <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000417> ;
                                                               owl:someValuesFrom <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200167>
                                                             ] ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000111> "loess transformation"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A loess transformation is a data transformation that takes as input a collection of real number pairs (x, y) and, after performing (one or more) loess fittings, utilizes the resulting curves to transform each (x, y) in the input into (x, y-f(x)) where f(x) is one of the fitted curves."@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en ,
                                                                                          "James Malone"@en ,
                                                                                          "Melanie Courtot"@en ,
                                                                                          "Philippe Rocca-Serra" ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "OTHER: Editor's generalization based on MGED Ontology term"@en ;
                                             rdfs:label "loess transformation"@en .


