                                                                                    ]
                                                                                    [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                                      owl:onProperty <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000417> ;
                                                                                      owl:someValuesFrom <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200179>
                                                                                    ]
                                                                                  ) ;
                                                               rdf:type owl:Class
                                                             ] ,
                                                             [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                               owl:onProperty <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000299> ;
                                                               owl:someValuesFrom <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000648>
                                                             ] ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000111> "discriminant function analysis"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125> ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "Discriminant function analysis is a form of discriminant analysis used to determine which variables discriminate between two or more naturally occurring groups. Analysis is used to determine which variable(s) are the best predictors of a particular outcome."@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "Tina Hernandez-Boussard"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "WEB: http://www.statsoft.com/textbook/stdiscan.html"@en ;
                                             rdfs:label "discriminant function analysis"@en .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200100
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200100> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                             rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200106> ,
                                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200171> ,
                                                             [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                               owl:onProperty <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000417> ;
                                                               owl:someValuesFrom <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200172>
                                                             ] ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000111> "canonical variate analysis"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125> ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "canonical variate analysis is a form of discriminant analysis that takes several continuous predictor variables and uses the entire set to predict several criterion variables, each of which is also continuous. CVA simultaneously calculates a linear composite of all x variables and  a linear composite of all y variables. Unlike other multivariate techniques, these weighted composites are derived in pairs. Each linear combination is called a canonical variate and takes the general linear form."@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "Tina Hernandez-Boussard"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000118> "CVA"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canonical_analysis"@en ;
                                             rdfs:label "canonical variate analysis"@en .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200101
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200101> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                             rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000663> ,
                                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200106> ,
                                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200175> ,
                                                             [ owl:intersectionOf ( [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                                      owl:onProperty <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000299> ;
                                                                                      owl:someValuesFrom <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000023>
                                                                                    ]
                                                                                    [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                                      owl:onProperty <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000417> ;
                                                                                      owl:someValuesFrom <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200179>
                                                                                    ]
                                                                                  ) ;
                                                               rdf:type owl:Class
                                                             ] ,
                                                             [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                               owl:onProperty <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000299> ;
                                                               owl:someValuesFrom <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000648>
                                                             ] ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000111> "linear discriminant functional analysis"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125> ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "Linear discriminant functional analysis (LDFA) is a multivariate technique used in special applications where there are several intact groups (random assignment may be impossible) and they have been measured on several independent measures. Thus, you will want to describe how these groups differ on the basis of these measures. In this case, classification and prediction is the main objective."@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "Tina Hernandez-Boussard"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PERSON: Tina Hernandez-Boussard"@en ;
                                             rdfs:label "linear discriminant functional analysis"@en .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200102
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200102> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                             rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200000> ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000111> "regression analysis method"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125> ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "Regression analysis is a descriptive statistics technique that examines the relation of a dependent variable (response variable) to specified independent variables (explanatory variables). Regression analysis can be used as a descriptive method of data analysis (such as curve fitting) without relying on any assumptions about underlying processes generating the data."@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "Tina Hernandez-Boussard"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "BOOK: Richard A. Berk, Regression Analysis: A Constructive Critique, Sage Publications (2004) 978-0761929048"@en ;
                                             rdfs:label "regression analysis method"@en .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200103
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200103> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                             rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200102> ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000111> "multiple linear regression analysis"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125> ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> """multiple linear regression is a regression method that models the relationship between a dependent variable Y, independent variables Xi, i = 1, ..., p, and a random term epsilon. The model can be written as
    Y = \\beta_0 + \\beta_1 X_1 + \\beta_2 X_2 + \\cdots +\\beta_p X_p + \\varepsilon
where \\beta_0 =  0 is the intercept (\"constant\" term), the \\beta_i s  are the respective parameters of independent variables, and p is the number of parameters to be estimated in the linear regression."""@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "Tina Hernandez-Boussard"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "WEB:http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linear_regression"@en ;
                                             rdfs:label "multiple linear regression analysis"@en .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200104
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200104> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                             rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200102> ,
                                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200175> ,
                                                             [ owl:intersectionOf ( [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                                      owl:onProperty <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000299> ;
                                                                                      owl:someValuesFrom <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000648>
                                                                                    ]
                                                                                    [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                                      owl:onProperty <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000417> ;
                                                                                      owl:someValuesFrom <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200178>
                                                                                    ]
                                                                                  ) ;
                                                               rdf:type owl:Class
                                                             ] ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000111> "principal component regression"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125> ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "The Principal Component Regression method is a regression analysis method that combines the Principal Component Analysis (PCA)spectral decomposition with an Inverse Least Squares (ILS) regression method to create a quantitative model for complex samples. Unlike quantitation methods based directly on Beer's Law which attempt to calculate the absorbtivity coefficients for the constituents of interest from a direct regression of the constituent concentrations onto the spectroscopic responses, the PCR method regresses the concentrations on the PCA scores."@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "Tina Hernandez-Boussard"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "WEB: : http://www.thermo.com/com/cda/resources/resources_detail/1,2166,13414,00.html"@en ;
                                             rdfs:label "principal component regression"@en .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200105
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200105> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                             rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200102> ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000111> "partial least square regression analysis"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125> ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> """Partial least squares regression is an extension of the multiple linear regression model (see, e.g., Multiple Regression or General Stepwise Regression). In its simplest form, a linear model specifies the (linear) relationship between a dependent (response) variable Y, and a set of predictor variables, the X's, so that
Y = b0 + b1X1 + b2X2 + ... + bpXp
In this equation b0 is the regression coefficient for the intercept and the bi values are the regression coefficients (for variables 1 through p) computed from the data."""@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "Tina Hernandez-Boussard"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000118> "PLS-RA"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "ARTICLE: de Jong, S. (1993). SIMPLS: An alternative approach to partial least squares regression. Chemometrics and Intelligent Laboratory Systems, 18: 251-263."@en ;
                                             rdfs:label "partial least square regression analysis"@en .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200106
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200106> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                             rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200000> ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000111> "discriminant analysis"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125> ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "Discriminant function analysis is used to determine which variables discriminate between two or more naturally occurring groups. Analysis is used to determine which variable(s) are the best predictors of a particular outcome."@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "Tina Hernandez-Boussard"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "WEB: http://www.statsoft.com/textbook/stdiscan.html"@en ;
                                             rdfs:label "discriminant analysis"@en .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200107
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200107> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                             rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200106> ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000111> "partial least square discriminant analysis"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125> ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "PLS Discriminant Analysis (PLS-DA) is a discriminant analysis performed in order to sharpen the separation between groups of observations, by hopefully rotating PCA (Principal Components Analysis) components such that a maximum separation among classes is obtained, and to understand which variables carry the class separating information."@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "James Malone"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000118> "PLS-DA"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "WEB: http://www.camo.com/rt/Resources/pls-da.html" ;
                                             rdfs:label "partial least square discriminant analysis"@en .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200108
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200108> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                             rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200169> ,
                                                             [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                               owl:onProperty <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000417> ;
                                                               owl:someValuesFrom <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200167>
                                                             ] ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000111> "eh transformation"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> "This type of transformation is typically used in flow cytometry."@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "An eh transformation is a data transformation obtained by applying the function EH described in what follows to a (one dimensional) real number input. EH(x)=exp(x*d/r)+b*(d/r)*x-1, if x>=0, and EH(x)=-exp(-x*d/r)+b*(d/r)*x+1, otherwise. Here exp denotes an exponential transformation and b, d, r are positive real constants with the objective of normalization."@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en ,
                                                                                          "Joseph Spliden"@en ,
                                                                                          "Ryan Brinkman"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "WEB: http://flowcyt.sourceforge.net/gating/latest.pdf"@en ;
                                             rdfs:label "eh transformation"@en .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200109
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200109> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                             rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200169> ,
                                                             [ owl:intersectionOf ( [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                                      owl:onProperty <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000299> ;
                                                                                      owl:someValuesFrom <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000451>
                                                                                    ]
                                                                                    [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                                      owl:onProperty <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000417> ;
                                                                                      owl:someValuesFrom <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200167>
                                                                                    ]
                                                                                  ) ;
                                                               rdf:type owl:Class
                                                             ] ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000111> "b transformation"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> "This type of transformation is typically used in flow cytometry."@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A b transformation is a data transformation obtained by applying the function B described in what follows to a (one dimensional) real number input. B(x)= a*exp(b*x)-c*exp(-d*x)+f, where exp denotes an exponential transformation and a, b, c, d, f are real constants with a, b, c, d positive with the objective of normalization."@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en ,
                                                                                          "Joseph Spliden"@en ,
                                                                                          "Ryan Brinkman"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "WEB: http://flowcyt.sourceforge.net/gating/latest.pdf"@en ;
                                             rdfs:label "b transformation"@en .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200110
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200110> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                             rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200169> ,
                                                             [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                               owl:onProperty <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000417> ;
                                                               owl:someValuesFrom <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200167>
                                                             ] ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000111> "s transformation"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> "This type of transformation is typically used in flow cytometry."@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "An s transformation is a data transformation obtained by applying the function S described in what follows to a (one dimensional) real number input. S(x)=T*exp(w-m)*(exp(x-w)-(p^2)*exp((w-x)/p)+p^2-1) if x>=w, S(x)=-S(w-x) otherwise; where exp denotes an exponential_transformations, 'p^' denotes the exponential transformation with base p; T, w, m, p are real constants with T, m, and p positive and w non-negative, and where w and p are related by w=2p*ln(p)(p+1) with the objective of normalization."@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en ,
                                                                                          "Joseph Spliden"@en ,
                                                                                          "Ryan Brinkman"@en ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "WEB: http://flowcyt.sourceforge.net/gating/latest.pdf"@en ;
                                             rdfs:label "s transformation"@en .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200111
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200111> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                             rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/COB_0000035> ,
                                                             [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                               owl:onProperty <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000293> ;
